1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Ah.

2
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:07,320
You're studying.

3
00:00:07,630 --> 00:00:08,450
Sorry.

4
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,599
It's fine. I'm just browsing.

5
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:11,730
Have a seat.

6
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:20,490
I went to see "Blueprint" today.

7
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:22,020
Again?

8
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:24,940
That's the third time.

9
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:31,650
And it made me really want to go see it.

10
00:00:32,070 --> 00:00:33,070
That island.

11
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:37,740
Is that why you mentioned a pilgrimage?

12
00:00:38,990 --> 00:00:39,990
Chiharu.

13
00:00:40,450 --> 00:00:43,390
Didn't you mention a pilgrimage
for "Sea of Light" before?

14
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:45,600
I suddenly remembered that,

15
00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:48,320
and I thought about taking my camera there.

16
00:00:49,290 --> 00:00:50,980
You mean to shoot a film?

17
00:00:51,170 --> 00:00:52,170
Here.

18
00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:54,020
Thanks.

19
00:00:56,470 --> 00:00:58,640
Since I have the study
abroad screening coming up,

20
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:03,100
I figured I might find
some good inspiration.

21
00:01:05,580 --> 00:01:06,140
Even though

22
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:08,000
I could go by myself,

23
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:10,020
it's more fun to have some company.

24
00:01:11,820 --> 00:01:13,620
That sounds like something
Akiyoshi would do.

25
00:01:13,990 --> 00:01:14,990
Really?

26
00:01:15,110 --> 00:01:16,110
Yeah.

27
00:01:17,020 --> 00:01:20,940
Acting on whatever comes to mind.
It feels like you live by your instincts.

28
00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:23,766
You're not complimenting me, are you?

29
00:01:23,790 --> 00:01:25,620
No, I meant it as a compliment, mostly.

30
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:29,000
I always overthink things before I act.

31
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:32,920
And I often end up making the wrong choice.

32
00:01:35,090 --> 00:01:36,610
That's not true.

33
00:01:39,260 --> 00:01:41,220
But we're college students now.

34
00:01:41,390 --> 00:01:44,190
If we keep taking it easy, we'll be
left behind in the blink of an eye.

35
00:01:45,820 --> 00:01:48,520
Yeah, you're right.

36
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,940
Anyway, you probably
have your own plans, Chiharu.

37
00:01:55,990 --> 00:01:59,760
Just decide on the pilgrimage
before summer break.

38
00:02:01,020 --> 00:02:02,830
Yeah, got it.

39
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:13,259
I'm gonna head back now.

40
00:02:13,260 --> 00:02:14,230
Huh? You're leaving already?

41
00:02:14,250 --> 00:02:15,960
I need to study for my exams too.

42
00:02:18,420 --> 00:02:19,420
Oh, right.

43
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:21,280
Should we invite Toda too?

44
00:02:21,470 --> 00:02:22,470
Huh?

45
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:26,730
Doesn't he really like Director Zaizen?

46
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:29,950
I feel like he'd know a lot of
details about the filming locations.

47
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:31,760
I don't know.

48
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:35,579
But before that, we need
to get through our exams.

49
00:02:35,580 --> 00:02:36,580
Yeah.

50
00:02:36,650 --> 00:02:38,070
See you at school.

51
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:39,320
I'm off.

52
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:56,460
A pilgrimage for "Blueprint."

53
00:02:57,630 --> 00:03:00,610
I've been too scared to invite Wataru.

54
00:03:01,660 --> 00:03:02,940
Even though I really want to go.

55
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:05,260
Even though it would be so much fun.

56
00:03:06,140 --> 00:03:07,140
I thought...

57
00:03:10,730 --> 00:03:12,560
we'd never see each other again.

58
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:15,330
That summer we went on the pilgrimage,

59
00:03:16,690 --> 00:03:18,500
I hurt Wataru.

60
00:03:20,030 --> 00:03:22,610
The closer I get to Wataru,

61
00:03:24,030 --> 00:03:25,550
the more my heart aches.

62
00:04:57,200 --> 00:05:02,500
"My Summer Of You"
(Episode 10)

63
00:05:03,420 --> 00:05:05,820
Come to think of it, you're
already twenty, right, Toda?

64
00:05:05,940 --> 00:05:07,940
Yeah, I just turned twenty last month.

65
00:05:08,180 --> 00:05:09,180
Oh.

66
00:05:09,260 --> 00:05:10,970
Let's go drinking next time.

67
00:05:11,220 --> 00:05:12,349
We'll invite Saito-san too.

68
00:05:12,350 --> 00:05:13,680
Oh, that's a great idea.

69
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:17,160
Let me think, when would be good?
A day when everyone is on shift.

70
00:05:20,340 --> 00:05:21,960
Oh, if it isn't Toda.

71
00:05:22,610 --> 00:05:23,610
Huh?

72
00:05:24,020 --> 00:05:25,639
So this is where you work part-time.

73
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:28,259
Yeah. Are you here for the next screening?

74
00:05:28,260 --> 00:05:29,260
Yeah.

75
00:05:29,440 --> 00:05:31,910
I got here too early, so I
was gonna come back later.

76
00:05:31,990 --> 00:05:32,990
But then I saw you here.

77
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:34,120
I see.

78
00:05:35,790 --> 00:05:36,790
Toda.

79
00:05:36,830 --> 00:05:37,830
Yeah?

80
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:41,560
The pilgrimage for "Blueprint."

81
00:05:42,130 --> 00:05:43,270
Do you want to go together?

82
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:44,920
Huh?

83
00:05:45,140 --> 00:05:47,990
Well, Chiharu and I are planning
to go during summer break.

84
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:50,320
Do you want to join us?

85
00:05:51,640 --> 00:05:52,640
I see...

86
00:05:53,220 --> 00:05:54,420
So that's how it is.

87
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:58,660
While I'm still in Japan, I really want
to visit that island no matter what.

88
00:05:59,610 --> 00:06:01,540
If you're interested,
just let Chiharu know.

89
00:06:05,070 --> 00:06:07,920
I'm gonna go wander
around outside for a bit.

90
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:09,260
See you later.

91
00:06:09,570 --> 00:06:10,570
Yeah.

92
00:06:16,720 --> 00:06:18,180
A friend of the handsome guy?

93
00:06:18,370 --> 00:06:19,720
Ah, yeah.

94
00:06:20,540 --> 00:06:23,900
So you're going on a pilgrimage
for "Blueprint" with him?

95
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:25,360
Huh?

96
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:28,180
Sorry, I overheard.

97
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:30,500
Ah, no.

98
00:06:31,180 --> 00:06:34,700
It seems he's decided to go with Chiharu,
so I won't crash their party.

99
00:06:34,890 --> 00:06:36,100
Oh...

100
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:42,416
By the way, there's no
time like the present.

101
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:44,000
Are you free tonight?

102
00:06:44,480 --> 00:06:48,299
To celebrate Toda-kun
turning twenty, cheers!

103
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:50,700
- Cheers!
- Thank you, everyone.

104
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:59,179
It's really nice to drink
with my seniors from work.

105
00:06:59,180 --> 00:07:00,920
So? Can you hold your liquor?

106
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:03,420
I'm gonna get really
good at it from now on.

107
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:04,860
So you're a lightweight.

108
00:07:04,861 --> 00:07:06,260
Don't push yourself.

109
00:07:06,580 --> 00:07:08,509
It's important to know your limits.

110
00:07:08,510 --> 00:07:10,010
Okay, I'll keep that in mind.

111
00:07:13,140 --> 00:07:14,420
Sorry for the wait.

112
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:16,269
Here are your appetizers and edamame.

113
00:07:16,270 --> 00:07:19,059
- Here we go.
- Looks delicious.

114
00:07:19,060 --> 00:07:20,350
Let's eat.

115
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:55,300
(If it's convenient, do you want to go
on the "Blueprint" pilgrimage together?)

116
00:08:11,150 --> 00:08:14,490
There's a real shortage
of handsome guys lately.

117
00:08:15,780 --> 00:08:18,040
Saito-san is already a little drunk.

118
00:08:18,580 --> 00:08:20,779
That's pretty harsh to
say right in front of us.

119
00:08:20,780 --> 00:08:22,250
Huh? Did I say something?

120
00:08:22,380 --> 00:08:23,380
No.

121
00:08:23,960 --> 00:08:26,670
In that case,
why don't you just watch more movies?

122
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,100
There are a lot of good
young actors these days.

123
00:08:29,140 --> 00:08:31,010
Young actors, huh.

124
00:08:36,980 --> 00:08:37,980
Oh, right.

125
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:39,420
He's not an actor, but...

126
00:08:39,540 --> 00:08:40,540
Toda-kun's...

127
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:41,950
Huh?

128
00:08:42,100 --> 00:08:45,020
Didn't Toda-kun's friend come by before?

129
00:08:45,260 --> 00:08:46,260
Ah...

130
00:08:47,280 --> 00:08:48,280
Chiharu...?

131
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:50,480
So his name is Chiharu.

132
00:08:50,620 --> 00:08:54,529
Tall, handsome,
elegant, and gentle.

133
00:08:54,530 --> 00:08:57,320
That kind of handsome
guy is totally my type.

134
00:08:57,570 --> 00:08:58,780
He's a classic type.

135
00:08:59,540 --> 00:09:02,040
But cute is still best, right?

136
00:09:02,260 --> 00:09:04,439
Once you think someone is cute,
it's game over.

137
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:06,339
That has nothing to do with
being handsome, does it?

138
00:09:06,340 --> 00:09:09,750
It does! Being handsome
and cute is the ultimate combo.

139
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:12,359
The ultimate combo, huh.

140
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:16,010
Where is the timeline where
I can date a handsome guy?

141
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:18,519
Ah, excuse me.

142
00:09:18,520 --> 00:09:20,259
- Coming.
- What do you want to drink?

143
00:09:20,260 --> 00:09:21,999
Huh? Huh? You're not calling me, are you?

144
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,140
No, you've got it wrong.

145
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:24,160
A phone is ringing.

146
00:09:25,060 --> 00:09:26,060
Hello.

147
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:29,519
Toda-kun, it's time to go home.

148
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:30,650
No.

149
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:34,440
It's no use. He won't wake up at all.

150
00:09:35,610 --> 00:09:38,650
He didn't even drink that much. I
didn't expect him to be such a lightweight.

151
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:42,080
Niimi-kun, can you take him home?

152
00:09:42,990 --> 00:09:43,990
I can...

153
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:48,380
Saito-san,
do you know where Toda lives?

154
00:09:48,920 --> 00:09:50,640
I wouldn't know without
asking the company.

155
00:09:50,710 --> 00:09:52,130
True.

156
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:55,630
If only he could at least
tell us where he lives...

157
00:09:57,090 --> 00:09:58,180
He's completely out.

158
00:10:00,280 --> 00:10:01,360
Is there nothing we can do?

159
00:10:07,310 --> 00:10:08,310
Huh?

160
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:11,860
It's Toda-kun's phone.

161
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:13,800
(Incoming Call: Saeki)

162
00:10:15,060 --> 00:10:17,780
Ah, excuse me, I'll take this.

163
00:10:21,800 --> 00:10:23,790
- Hello?
- Hello?

164
00:10:24,490 --> 00:10:25,490
Huh?

165
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:27,700
(In Call: Wataru)

166
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:32,040
May I ask who's calling?

167
00:10:32,790 --> 00:10:34,170
Sorry for answering so suddenly.

168
00:10:34,380 --> 00:10:37,900
I'm Niimi, a coworker from
Toda-kun's part-time job.

169
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:43,160
Ah, Niimi-san.
From the movie theater...?

170
00:10:43,430 --> 00:10:44,430
Yes.

171
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:46,600
Ah, our staff was just
having some drinks together.

172
00:10:46,680 --> 00:10:49,520
But Toda-kun is in no condition
to answer the phone right now.

173
00:10:50,020 --> 00:10:51,520
So I answered it for him.

174
00:10:53,110 --> 00:10:55,130
Huh? What's going on?

175
00:10:56,660 --> 00:10:57,660
Ah.

176
00:10:57,900 --> 00:10:58,900
Is he passed out?

177
00:10:59,620 --> 00:11:00,700
Completely passed out.

178
00:11:03,880 --> 00:11:07,410
Toda, wake up.

179
00:11:08,330 --> 00:11:09,710
Hey, seriously.

180
00:11:10,460 --> 00:11:11,280
Excuse me.

181
00:11:11,460 --> 00:11:12,750
I'm Saeki from the phone call just now.

182
00:11:12,760 --> 00:11:14,329
Thank you for coming all this way...

183
00:11:14,330 --> 00:11:15,400
Not at all, we're the ones
who should apologize.

184
00:11:15,420 --> 00:11:18,759
He shouldn't have had that much to drink,
but he won't wake up at all.

185
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:22,050
Ah, something similar happened before.
He should be fine.

186
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:24,679
I'll let him rest here for a bit,
then take a taxi back with him.

187
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:29,299
I'm pretty worried too. Why don't I
ride in the taxi with you to drop him off?

188
00:11:29,300 --> 00:11:30,579
No, no, it's fine.

189
00:11:30,580 --> 00:11:32,139
- But...
- Come on, Saito-san.

190
00:11:32,140 --> 00:11:34,000
So comfortable.

191
00:11:34,520 --> 00:11:36,120
Such a familiar voice.

192
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:38,360
Let's go. We'll leave the rest to him.

193
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:39,559
Thank you, then.

194
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:40,569
Thank you all so much.

195
00:11:40,570 --> 00:11:41,420
Will you be okay?

196
00:11:41,421 --> 00:11:42,909
Yes, we'll be fine.

197
00:11:42,910 --> 00:11:44,120
So handsome.

198
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:52,020
Seriously. You're such a lightweight.

199
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:08,060
Ah... I really want to see Chiharu.

200
00:12:16,110 --> 00:12:17,650
Ah, you're awake?

201
00:12:18,370 --> 00:12:20,070
Huh? It's Chiharu.

202
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:21,550
Yeah.

203
00:12:21,670 --> 00:12:22,820
I came to pick you up.

204
00:12:24,030 --> 00:12:25,030
Hmm...?

205
00:12:25,530 --> 00:12:27,280
Where am I?

206
00:12:27,910 --> 00:12:30,620
A park near the place
you were just drinking at.

207
00:12:30,830 --> 00:12:34,170
Huh? Did I fall asleep again?

208
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:36,250
Yeah.

209
00:12:37,750 --> 00:12:39,960
Are you okay?
Feeling sick at all?

210
00:12:40,420 --> 00:12:47,760
I feel like I'm floating.
It's actually pretty nice.

211
00:12:48,730 --> 00:12:51,640
Then again, this has to be a dream.

212
00:12:52,100 --> 00:12:53,100
Huh?

213
00:12:54,870 --> 00:12:58,230
Because I heard your voice.

214
00:12:58,320 --> 00:13:02,530
I was just thinking about how much I
wanted to see you, and then you appeared.

215
00:13:06,450 --> 00:13:09,870
I'm glad to hear that.

216
00:13:14,040 --> 00:13:16,170
Hey, come here.

217
00:13:16,710 --> 00:13:17,710
Hmm?

218
00:13:17,850 --> 00:13:19,170
Seriously, come a little closer.

219
00:13:19,920 --> 00:13:20,800
Uh, like this?

220
00:13:20,801 --> 00:13:22,689
Closer. Come a little closer.

221
00:13:22,690 --> 00:13:23,690
- A little closer?
- Yeah.

222
00:13:28,180 --> 00:13:29,510
What are you doing?

223
00:13:30,370 --> 00:13:31,450
This is amazing.

224
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:33,180
Even the touch feels so real.

225
00:13:38,990 --> 00:13:41,400
I hate to interrupt your sweet dream,

226
00:13:41,530 --> 00:13:42,966
but we should head back.
Come on, get up.

227
00:13:42,990 --> 00:13:43,750
Got it.

228
00:13:43,810 --> 00:13:45,360
I'm getting up.
I'm up.

229
00:13:51,410 --> 00:13:52,760
Um... Wataru.

230
00:13:53,250 --> 00:13:54,250
Yeah?

231
00:13:59,630 --> 00:14:02,250
You're free to drink with whoever you want.

232
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:04,696
But if you're drinking
with anyone other than me,

233
00:14:04,720 --> 00:14:07,220
I'd really appreciate it
if you could hold back a little.

234
00:14:08,410 --> 00:14:09,510
Hold back?

235
00:14:11,140 --> 00:14:13,910
Because I don't want anyone
else to see you so defenseless.

236
00:14:16,690 --> 00:14:19,060
I'd only ever show that
side of me to you anyway.

237
00:14:22,430 --> 00:14:26,070
You're going to get me hooked
on you. That's a real problem.

238
00:14:36,580 --> 00:14:37,370
Huh?

239
00:14:37,371 --> 00:14:40,210
Nothing. You're just amazing.

240
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,210
Huh? Amazing?

241
00:14:42,750 --> 00:14:44,459
A champion.

242
00:14:44,460 --> 00:14:45,030
Why a champion?

243
00:14:45,031 --> 00:14:46,409
Champion. Champ, champ~.

244
00:14:46,410 --> 00:14:47,609
You're totally slurring your words.

245
00:14:47,610 --> 00:14:51,600
A timeline where you can date a hot guy
like that actually exists in reality, right?

246
00:14:51,720 --> 00:14:55,429
Why can't I ever
cross paths with that timeline?

247
00:14:55,430 --> 00:14:58,130
I've been thinking about this.

248
00:14:58,170 --> 00:14:59,410
- It just feels so unfair.
- Ah.

249
00:15:01,710 --> 00:15:04,069
Whoa, seriously.

250
00:15:04,070 --> 00:15:05,400
Ah, I forgot.

251
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:06,440
Thanks for the help.

252
00:15:07,030 --> 00:15:08,530
Huh...

253
00:15:09,450 --> 00:15:13,870
Ah, water in a dream tastes so good.

254
00:15:16,370 --> 00:15:18,790
I'm going to check the road.
Wait here for me.

255
00:15:28,340 --> 00:15:29,340
What's wrong?

256
00:15:30,570 --> 00:15:31,570
No.

257
00:15:33,030 --> 00:15:34,350
Where are you going?

258
00:15:35,390 --> 00:15:37,290
I'm just going to check
the road over there.

259
00:15:37,310 --> 00:15:38,680
We need to call a cab.

260
00:15:40,480 --> 00:15:41,500
But...

261
00:15:44,050 --> 00:15:47,410
Because if I take my eyes off you for a
second, you'll wander off to who knows where.

262
00:15:49,860 --> 00:15:51,050
Wataru...

263
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:08,060
We're outside, you know.

264
00:16:09,380 --> 00:16:10,550
It's just a dream anyway.

265
00:16:13,110 --> 00:16:14,530
Then let's do it again.

266
00:16:34,350 --> 00:16:36,070
How am I supposed to pay him back for this?

267
00:16:40,730 --> 00:16:42,760
I'm so sorry for causing you trouble.

268
00:16:43,460 --> 00:16:44,850
Don't worry about it.

269
00:16:44,870 --> 00:16:47,106
When you first start drinking,
it's hard to pace yourself.

270
00:16:47,130 --> 00:16:47,930
I'm sorry.

271
00:16:47,931 --> 00:16:49,851
Niimi-san,
thanks for holding onto my phone, too.

272
00:16:50,130 --> 00:16:51,260
Don't mention it.

273
00:16:51,410 --> 00:16:53,309
I should be apologizing for
noticing so late. Sorry about that.

274
00:16:53,310 --> 00:16:56,050
Not at all.
Thank you both so much for everything.

275
00:16:56,350 --> 00:16:59,740
If you're going to thank anyone,
you should thank Chiharu-kun, too.

276
00:17:00,680 --> 00:17:01,680
I will.

277
00:17:02,230 --> 00:17:03,770
I definitely will.

278
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:08,570
Anyway, let's drink
together again sometime.

279
00:17:09,850 --> 00:17:10,850
Sounds good.

280
00:17:16,230 --> 00:17:18,619
Huh? Guchi?

281
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:19,699
(New message from Guchi)

282
00:17:19,700 --> 00:17:20,700
Hmm?

283
00:17:20,990 --> 00:17:22,450
Comfort me.

284
00:17:22,790 --> 00:17:23,790
(Teary eyes)

285
00:17:33,030 --> 00:17:34,320
Is it really hot today?

286
00:17:34,670 --> 00:17:36,510
It's pure torture for
someone with a hangover.

287
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:37,800
You went drinking?

288
00:17:38,510 --> 00:17:39,890
I got a little carried away.

289
00:17:40,916 --> 00:17:42,591
I went drinking with some
people from my department,

290
00:17:42,868 --> 00:17:44,796
and there was this guy who
could drink anyone under the table.

291
00:17:44,830 --> 00:17:46,036
I ended up getting
dragged down with him.

292
00:17:46,060 --> 00:17:48,140
Akiyoshi, aren't you a
pretty good drinker yourself?

293
00:17:48,690 --> 00:17:49,690
Yeah.

294
00:17:50,150 --> 00:17:52,170
I guess I'm alright.

295
00:17:52,430 --> 00:17:56,660
But I heard I spent yesterday hiding
in a corner, drinking all by myself.

296
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:57,950
That's hilarious.

297
00:17:58,870 --> 00:18:00,030
You don't remember?

298
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:02,080
Nope, not at all.

299
00:18:03,830 --> 00:18:07,270
But don't they say your true
self comes out when you're drunk?

300
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:10,790
No.

301
00:18:10,791 --> 00:18:13,626
Because if I take my eyes off you for a
second, you'll wander off to who knows where.

302
00:18:13,650 --> 00:18:15,220
Stay here.

303
00:18:16,190 --> 00:18:21,240
So maybe I have
some subconscious desire to be alone.

304
00:18:23,590 --> 00:18:27,479
Oh right, I ran into Toda at
the movie theater the other day.

305
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:29,666
I went ahead and invited him
to go on the pilgrimage with us.

306
00:18:29,690 --> 00:18:30,690
Huh?

307
00:18:32,150 --> 00:18:33,150
Huh?

308
00:18:36,230 --> 00:18:39,630
I told him to contact you if he
could make it. Is that a problem?

309
00:18:40,190 --> 00:18:42,410
No, I'm just a little surprised.

310
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:43,830
Hmm...

311
00:18:45,120 --> 00:18:46,120
I see.

312
00:18:52,590 --> 00:18:54,380
I got my heart broken.

313
00:18:57,990 --> 00:18:59,469
Guys.

314
00:18:59,470 --> 00:19:01,430
Hurry up and comfort me.

315
00:19:02,370 --> 00:19:04,680
- Rough day.
- Rough day.

316
00:19:05,490 --> 00:19:06,490
Rough day.

317
00:19:06,600 --> 00:19:10,060
Is it that upperclassman
you said you had a good feeling about?

318
00:19:11,070 --> 00:19:13,570
I thought things were going well,

319
00:19:14,440 --> 00:19:20,029
but before I could even make a move,
the romance was already over.

320
00:19:20,030 --> 00:19:23,869
Is it the classic cliché
where she already has a boyfriend?

321
00:19:23,870 --> 00:19:27,040
Don't say it so casually.

322
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:31,669
It was a huge blow to me.

323
00:19:31,670 --> 00:19:32,670
So that's what it was.

324
00:19:34,630 --> 00:19:35,630
And then...

325
00:19:36,050 --> 00:19:40,630
She's quitting her part-time job
because she found full-time work.

326
00:19:42,090 --> 00:19:45,100
I figured I'd never see her again,

327
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:48,180
Oh, so it's finally game over?

328
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:51,100
so I confessed my feelings.

329
00:19:51,890 --> 00:19:52,890
Huh?

330
00:19:53,060 --> 00:19:54,230
Seriously?

331
00:19:54,470 --> 00:19:56,570
So... what did she say?

332
00:19:56,710 --> 00:19:58,940
Even though she let me down easy,

333
00:19:59,030 --> 00:20:01,086
it's not something I can
just brush off with a 'so what'.

334
00:20:01,110 --> 00:20:04,280
If you knew you had no chance,
why did you even confess?

335
00:20:04,320 --> 00:20:07,369
It's not about having
a chance or not, okay?

336
00:20:07,370 --> 00:20:08,790
What do you mean?

337
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:10,960
Because,

338
00:20:14,030 --> 00:20:16,380
no matter how much I like her,

339
00:20:16,750 --> 00:20:20,260
if I don't say it out loud, to her,

340
00:20:20,590 --> 00:20:24,010
my feelings simply don't exist.

341
00:20:24,890 --> 00:20:26,640
It's just nothing. A void.

342
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:30,640
Nothing...

343
00:20:31,790 --> 00:20:35,310
Isn't that incredibly lonely?

344
00:20:38,940 --> 00:20:45,510
Thanks to her, I actually
started to like this job.

345
00:20:48,030 --> 00:20:49,910
So rather than a confession,

346
00:20:50,830 --> 00:20:52,960
I really just wanted to show my gratitude.

347
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,420
That's what I thought.

348
00:20:57,770 --> 00:21:01,630
So I'm really glad I said it.

349
00:21:07,430 --> 00:21:09,639
Don't you agree, Wataru?

350
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:11,680
Oh, are you the clingy
type when you're drunk?

351
00:21:12,940 --> 00:21:16,500
No, I think it's super impressive
that you were able to say it properly.

352
00:21:20,390 --> 00:21:22,650
That was really cool, Guchi.

353
00:21:23,450 --> 00:21:24,450
Wataru.

354
00:21:25,010 --> 00:21:27,010
We're best friends for life, you bastard.

355
00:21:27,490 --> 00:21:29,709
What about me, you jerk?

356
00:21:29,710 --> 00:21:32,230
You too, you jerk.

357
00:21:32,620 --> 00:21:34,830
You guys really haven't changed.

358
00:21:34,870 --> 00:21:36,420
You're a good friend, too.

359
00:21:36,670 --> 00:21:37,540
What are you doing?

360
00:21:37,541 --> 00:21:39,380
It's just the alcohol talking.

361
00:21:39,920 --> 00:21:42,089
Oh crap, crap, crap, crap, crap.

362
00:21:42,090 --> 00:21:43,590
Seriously, you're pushing your luck.

363
00:21:44,850 --> 00:21:46,639
Alright, let's toast.

364
00:21:46,640 --> 00:21:47,640
Cheers.

365
00:22:08,570 --> 00:22:09,570
Chiharu?

366
00:22:10,210 --> 00:22:11,210
Wataru.

367
00:22:12,240 --> 00:22:13,540
Sorry it's so late.

368
00:22:14,410 --> 00:22:16,000
I have something I want to tell you.

369
00:22:16,370 --> 00:22:17,500
Is now a good time?

370
00:22:19,670 --> 00:22:22,020
Chiharu, look outside.

371
00:22:22,920 --> 00:22:23,920
Huh?

372
00:22:33,100 --> 00:22:33,930
Hey.

373
00:22:34,060 --> 00:22:35,100
What's up?

374
00:22:35,730 --> 00:22:37,730
I have something to tell you.

375
00:22:38,020 --> 00:22:39,060
Me too.

376
00:22:41,850 --> 00:22:42,850
I see.

377
00:22:44,710 --> 00:22:46,750
Can I go first?

378
00:22:48,280 --> 00:22:49,010
Yeah.

379
00:22:49,160 --> 00:22:50,160
Of course.

380
00:22:54,370 --> 00:22:55,890
During summer break...

381
00:23:01,290 --> 00:23:04,230
I want to go on the pilgrimage
for 'Blueprint' with you.

382
00:23:11,760 --> 00:23:14,070
I was just about to say
the exact same thing.

383
00:23:20,590 --> 00:23:21,590
Really?

384
00:23:25,050 --> 00:23:26,460
That's great.

385
00:23:27,950 --> 00:23:29,860
Yeah, it is.

386
00:23:33,930 --> 00:23:36,430
To pick up where our
story left off that summer,

387
00:23:36,580 --> 00:23:39,430
we're going on a pilgrimage again.

388
00:23:40,830 --> 00:23:43,250
If it's in a summer just like that one,

389
00:23:44,210 --> 00:23:46,310
I feel like I'll be able
to convey everything.

390
00:23:48,470 --> 00:23:49,809
Want to grab something to eat?

391
00:23:49,810 --> 00:23:52,010
Ah, let's go get some beef bowls.

392
00:24:45,690 --> 00:24:46,610
(Next Episode Preview)
Let's go together.

393
00:24:46,610 --> 00:24:47,610
Yeah, it's fine.

394
00:24:47,630 --> 00:24:48,830
I'll never... with Wataru again.

395
00:24:48,850 --> 00:24:51,240
But you're going to
disappear again, aren't you?

396
00:24:51,390 --> 00:24:52,400
It fell.

397
00:24:52,850 --> 00:24:55,706
I came here because I wanted to properly
convey these complicated feelings to you.

398
00:24:55,730 --> 00:24:56,730
Wataru.

399
00:24:57,170 --> 00:24:58,170
Wataru.
